&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;To escort the Grail Reliquary, we needed some fanatic pilgrims. I wanted them to look like religious cultists, with some serious gesture and some stuff for in-battle devotions. I had in mind the picture of fat friars and fighter-monks in dresses and I wanted to be able to customize each minis but with a unique body basis.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;The body I did has a very neutral standing which allows many custom stuff like a staff, a standard, a scroll, a sword, a club and of course, a shield. You can use any heads of my bretonnian set on it (the archers&amp;#39; hooded one, the errants&amp;#39; hairless one or even any of you own). For the picture, I did many pilgrims using legit heads, printed heads and even a greenstuff made head). The stuff used to custom is mainly handmade with toothpicks, greenstuff or comes from legit kits.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;A body takes 1h15 to be printed.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;You&amp;#39;ll find the reliquary there:
